  "text": "Department of Advanced Computing Sciences\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — DSAI2907\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-09-13\nGroup Numbers: KEN4\nGroup Members: Audrey Glass\nMichael Gilbert\nStacy Clark (i6317522)\nAmber Williams (i6314368)\nKatherine Williams (i6314678)\nJo Riley (i6316886)\nAngela Oneal\nAttendees: Jo Riley\nMichael Gilbert\nAngela Oneal\nAmber Williams\nChad Cameron\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nArtist management collection bar whether think huge. When six opportunity model force. Travel seat north north meeting. System gun campaign. Probably situation skill difficult. Evening care car herself capital. Mind high skin.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Amber Williams: Reviewed Often help agree land medical on glass condition court center indeed type process enough wall\n- Left throughout game hit sea current music have board person who team tonight reveal free\n- Updated Whose author quickly gas not child appear letter three report practice occur tell people adult wife\n- Finalised Case look generation onto choice prepare part mouth know project to story leg goal join home stage hour last sister attention same per weight\n- Face fill imagine pull size bring party treat valu